          <Pad Id="3sYROub7a9zMPweo2NtwTy" Bounds="85,776,830,230" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Points are relative to the origin of the parent, in units of the Renderer Space (1 unit = 100 DIP, origin top left). The shapes here are built around 0, 0 and moved with Transform (Translation): Transform acts around the origin, so a shape built around its own centre also rotates and scales around it.&#xD;&#xA;- Fill Rule decides which areas of a self-intersecting outline count as inside: NonZero fills every area the outline encloses at least once, EvenOdd leaves out the areas enclosed an even number of times, here the centre of the pentagram.&#xD;&#xA;- A Polygon is filled by default and has no stroke (Stroke Width 0). Defaults follow Skia: Join Miter, Fill Rule NonZero (Skia: Winding).&#xD;&#xA;- A shape holds at most 8190 points; more are cut off and the node shows a warning. Points that change every frame cost real time: stay below about 4000 points, or move the shape with Transform instead.&#xD;&#xA;- Connect it to Renderer [Qt] or a Group [Qt].">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
